{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR7, current names and install guides. Head f5b6bc90fc95d040cb68fed188111dba016a3c28, branch request/br7-current-names-20261027. Main 59a19054 is the merge base. The delta is 28 paths, 1,227 insertions and 115 deletions. Review request 4acb02e5, checker promise d8358050, request 8c3af8ba, builder promise aaf158b9, planner ruling 7a2be78b. Primary artifact 34d830be (the PD-2 note), first of 34. gs inspect shows it resting on promise aaf158b9, request 8c3af8ba and ruling 7a2be78b.\n\nRead order: the note in full; 8c3af8ba and 7a2be78b; the production diff (commands.ts, line.ts, mcp service.ts and platform register.ts); install-cohort.test.ts and the shared historical-plan helper; the guide changes; the raw control record; the gate record; the manifest and the sealed directory. I did not run any suite again.\n\nAcceptance (8c3af8ba, within 7a2be78b):\n1. The CLI offers only admitted families. CREATION_INSTALL_COHORTS names five: application, archive-device-application, archive-device-publication, archive-certified-rules and hardened-certified-rules. Their registers are exactly Scope's CREATION_COHORTS (creation-lineage.ts:21), and the owning test compares the two sets. The usage lines for install and install --plan list only those five.\n2. A fresh plan on a historical selector refuses in cohortPlan before signing or plan storage, with a fixed message naming the five. It is reached only after an explicit --cohort or --register-policy open, which maps to archive-device-application, an admitted family. Omitting --cohort keeps the existing default path, unchanged.\n3. Saved plans still read. Historical names remain in INSTALL_COHORTS, so install --planned recognizes them, and the execute path does not consult the creation list. The original definition, signature, register ID and deadline are kept, and the expired-plan message names a current family. The eight fixture owners now build retained historical custody through one test-only helper, keep their exact pins and delivery assertions, and get no Native receipt from it.\n4. Guides. No active guide, help line or MCP description instructs a historical cohort. I grepped docs, apps and examples for \"--cohort \u003chistorical name\u003e\" and found none. The remaining mentions are labelled \"historical\", for example \"an existing historical trusted-application room\". The MCP create example now names platform:register@18, the register of the default archive-device-publication cohort. docs/mcp-tools.json is regenerated. REGISTER (platform:register@2) keeps its value with an accurate \"historical\" comment. docs/testing.md drops the helper name that does not exist.\n5. Nothing else moves: no creation default, pin, archive cut, allowance, route or deployment change.\n\nControl (raw output read). Disabling the new creation guard (if (false)) makes \"fresh creation offers exactly admitted families and refuses historical selectors before custody\" fail (code 0 against 2; 1 failed, 4 skipped), and the file is restored. The first control exited 2 before running any test, so it is inconclusive, and the note says so.\n\nValidation:\n- The ordinary gate at 10e89e18 (tree 7f13a3a1) passed: clean before and after, no signal, Node 66, Counting 55, plain 2,864 passed and 1 skipped, Native 796 passed and 2 skipped, 0 unhandled. The note gives 1,177.6 s wall and 2,414.9 s child CPU (one run).\n- After the gate only the note and the manifest change, so the documents-only rule applies.\n- The manifest verifies against the sealed directory: 170 files, 0 bad, nothing writable, SHA256SUMS all OK.\n- check-notes 59a19054..f5b6bc90 reports 0 warnings, and git diff --check is clean.\n- check-doc-links on an exported tree of the head: 712 relative links checked, 0 broken.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The offer is a five-name list in the CLI, pinned by test to the server's admitted cohorts, so the runtime client does not import the Native admission graph. Recognition of historical plans is unchanged.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A historical selector now refuses before any signing, so the CLI can no longer produce a fresh founding entry that the server refuses. Retained custody keeps its exact bytes.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. Nit: line.ts:106 still checks the cohort flag against 13 hand-written names, which repeat the keys of INSTALL_COHORTS. An Object.hasOwn check on that table would keep one list. The shared test helper removes eight copies of historical setup.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head f5b6bc90. The builder lands. The landing closes BR7 request 8c3af8ba. No builder deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:34d830bebc9fb0e8331a16683316d8bb00d23be2","binding":"assigned","head":"f5b6bc90fc95d040cb68fed188111dba016a3c28","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d83580506a1385e23b1123d2d2be5b3cbf5af165\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aaf158b95dbdbbd067a6d559d2ec349d22d904d3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ef5a5923f5b42c70e013954a3f39ecdc7a88aa45","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}